The whole union_sockaddr to getsockname(), getpeername(), recvfrom() and recvmsg(),
not its member struct sockaddr (azsupport/ports, 27.11.2026): with _FORTIFY_SOURCE=2
the <ssp/socket.h> of FreeBSD checks the length of the address against
__builtin_object_size(address, 1), which GCC takes for the 16 bytes of that member
(clang, through the inline functions of <ssp/socket.h>, for the whole object or
nothing), so that built by GCC 16 (Mk/Uses/azgcc.mk) each of these calls ends in
__chk_fail(), as getsockname() of the _socket module of Python 3.12 did (prog-bench
run 45935459608). The same address, so the same calls for clang.

